meta {
  name: 02 Callback (not independently testable)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/callback?code=placeholder&state=placeholder
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  NOT independently testable as a saved request -- OpenEMR mints `code` and
  `state` fresh, single-use, and tied to a specific browser session mid-login.
  There is no way to produce valid values without actually completing a real
  login first, and at that point OpenEMR's own redirect already calls this
  URL for you; you would never construct this URL by hand in real use.

  What running this AS SAVED (placeholder values) actually proves: a clean,
  fail-closed 400 --
    {"detail": "Unrecognized or expired login attempt (bad/stale state)."}
  -- confirmed live 2026-09-19/20 -- rather than a 500 or, worse, a silent
  success. That's still a real, useful regression check: a broken /callback
  should reject an invalid/stale code+state pair cleanly, not crash or grant
  a session it shouldn't.

  To see /callback actually succeed (set a real copilot_session cookie),
  complete a real login through a browser -- see bruno/README.md. There is
  no way to script the success path here.
}
